 "phase": "M3 (memory): compressed sprite sheets kept at their own size; sound bytes read without caching",
 "change": "OriginalBitmapBytes keeps a copy of the compressor's output at its own size: the output array kept the capacity reserved for it (an eighth of the input, or more after growing), 130 MB allocated for 52 MB of compressed sheets. The audio backend's conversion reads its record's bytes with bytes(in:), which copies them without caching the whole array in the record as the bytes getter did (L8's +12 MB).",
 "profile": "malloc_history at body 600 after L7: OriginalLZ4.compress output 129.6 MB in 712 allocations; after M3 77.5 MB (catalog 56.3, startup 21.2)",
 "review": "not delegated: a copy of the same bytes at their size and the record's non-caching read of the same bytes (values identical by construction); the codec tests cover the held capacity",
 "notes": "A probe in the worktree with M3 and M4a (shared Stage pages) showed a small, noisy Mac change; the gate's interleaved A/B measured -62 MB on the A12 and -65 MB on the Mac. M4a is shelved: the Stage loader's initialisation writes every page of the ~52 stages the catalog defines, so shared pages saved 87 -> 80 MB only. The harness now keeps the full dumpsys meminfo and smaps_rollup at body N.",
